      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Two series of aromatic compounds with perfluoroalkyl (RF ) groups of increasing length, 1,3,5,7-naphthalene(RF )4 and 1,3,5,7,9-corannulene(RF )5 , have been prepared and their electronic properties studied by low-temperature photoelectron spectroscopy (PES) (for gas-phase electron affinity measurements). These and many related compounds were also studied by DFT calculations. The data demonstrate unambiguously that the electron-withdrawing ability of RF substituents increases significantly and uniformly from CF3 to C2 F5 to n-C3 F7 to n-C4 F9 ."
      },
